# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ORDERING IS LOAD-BEARING BELOW THIS POINT.
# .dockerignore uses last-match-wins: a pattern lower in this file overrides
# an earlier one for the same path. The negation below MUST stay the very
# last skill-related rule in this file — if you append a new broad exclude
# pattern (e.g. "**/*.md" or "**/*.sh") anywhere after it, it will silently
# re-exclude backend/system_skills/** with NO error signal (the seeder is
# fail-soft: it logs and continues, and the healthcheck only probes `/`).
# Do not move this block back up, and do not add new ignore rules below it
# without re-verifying `docker compose build backend` still ships
# backend/system_skills/**/SKILL.md (see OQ-7 in .claude/specs/skills-boosted/plan.md).
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Skill packages must ship in the image — the seeder reads SKILL.md at runtime (OQ-7).
!backend/system_skills/**

# Hardening: the patterns above (.env, *.log, __pycache__/, *.pyc, .git/) are
# root-anchored (no "**/" prefix) so they only match at the build-context
# root — a .env/.log/.pyc/.git dropped anywhere nested under backend/
# (including under backend/system_skills/) would ship into the image without
# these. Placed after the negation above (ordering matters, see comment) so
# they still win over it for these specific secret/artifact patterns while
# leaving the rest of backend/system_skills/** untouched.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.log
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.git/
